{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791779014,"nonce":"LMuHunLg2leVq5gC2OVNpc0HcU4=","title":"Spec: extension packet buttons on job forms and applied-on-submit","message":"User request 2026-10-11 (after specs 019-021, before 0f9f307 other-provider models): 1) generate a tailored resume or cover letter from the extension for the job being viewed; 2) the generate options appear as small buttons or icons on the matching fields of the job application form (resume upload, cover letter field), like Jobright's Customize button; 3) when the user clicks the form's submit, the extension tells jobhunter the user applied (records the applied event; never submits itself). This pulls part of spec 017 phase 2 forward; user decision implies the phase 2 gate (8 ready packets in 4 weeks) is waived for these three features. Needs a spec addendum covering host permissions/content scripts on ATS hosts vs activeTab, attaching a generated file to a file input (or offering download/copy), Jobright coexistence, never-store fields, submit detection without false positives (validation errors, multi-page forms), spend confirmation for drafting, and privacy.","files":null}]}